import interaction.dl

to draw the UI popup in {a pointer to UI view:view} on {UI frame:frame}:
    set owner to view's popup
    if owner = @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI layout):
        return nothing
    if (the UI element (owner's node) is enabled in (view's instance)) = false:
        dismiss the UI popup in view
        return nothing
    refresh UI popup choices in view
    set anchor to owner's painted bounds
    paint UI choice popover (the address of (view's popup choices)) anchored at anchor within (the UI viewport bounds in view) using (the UI popup font in view) styled (the UI popup appearance in view) on frame
